---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { OS, pct } from '../../lib/oversub';

const faqs = [
  {
    name: "When is the deadline to apply for primary school in England?",
    text: "The national closing date for primary school (Reception) applications in England is 15 January. For September 2027 entry the deadline is 15 January 2027, a Friday. An application received after that date is a late application, and the council normally deals with it after the on-time applications."
  },
  {
    name: "When is the deadline to apply for secondary school in England?",
    text: "The national closing date for secondary school (Year 7) applications in England is 31 October. For September 2027 entry the deadline is 31 October 2026, a Saturday. An application received after that date is a late application, and the council normally deals with it after the on-time applications."
  },
  {
    name: "When is National Offer Day for primary school?",
    text: "National Offer Day for primary school is 16 April, or the next working day if that date falls on a weekend or bank holiday. For September 2027 entry, 16 April 2027 is a Friday, so offers are made on Friday 16 April 2027. Your council sets the date by which you must accept or decline, so check your offer letter."
  },
  {
    name: "When is National Offer Day for secondary school?",
    text: "National Offer Day for secondary school is 1 March, or the next working day if that date falls on a weekend or bank holiday. For September 2027 entry, 1 March 2027 is a Monday, so offers are made on Monday 1 March 2027. Your council sets the date by which you must accept or decline, so check your offer letter."
  },
  {
    name: "What is the appeal deadline for a refused school place?",
    text: "Each admission authority sets its own deadline for lodging an appeal, but it must allow at least 20 school days from the date you are told your application was unsuccessful. The date is in your offer letter or on the council's website. For applications made on time, the appeal must then be heard within 40 school days of that lodging deadline."
  },
  {
    name: "When do 11+ grammar school tests take place?",
    text: "Grammar school 11+ tests typically take place in September or October of Year 6, and in some areas in Year 5, roughly a year before the child would start secondary school. Registration usually opens in May or June. The exact dates vary by school and consortium, so check with the individual grammar school or local consortium by April each year."
  },
  {
    name: "What happens if I miss the school application deadline?",
    text: "An application received after the national closing date but before the autumn term of the entry year starts is a late application. The council normally deals with late applications after all on-time applications, so your preferred schools may already be full. Many councils accept a late application as on time where there is a good reason, such as a recent move to the area or a serious illness. Contact your council as soon as possible. A school cannot refuse a place solely because you applied later than other applicants."
  },
  {
    name: "How does in-year admissions work?",
    text: "In-year admissions apply when a family needs a school place outside the normal admissions round, for example after moving to a new area during the school year. You apply to the local authority or directly to the school, depending on the school type, at any point in the school year. The School Admissions Code says the outcome should be sent in writing within 10 school days if possible, and no later than 15 school days. If there is no place, you can ask to go on the waiting list."
  },
  {
    name: "What is the deadline to accept or decline a school offer?",
    text: "The School Admissions Code does not set a single national date. Your council sets the response deadline and states it in your offer letter, so check it as soon as the offer arrives. If you do not respond by the deadline, the offer may be withdrawn. Respond promptly, even if you plan to appeal or join a waiting list."
  },
  {
    name: "Can I change my school preferences after submitting my application?",
    text: "Most councils let you change your preferences up to the closing date. After the deadline, changes are normally accepted only in exceptional circumstances, such as a house move. Contact your council admissions team straight away if your circumstances change after you apply."
  },
  {
    name: "What if my child has an Education, Health and Care Plan (EHCP)?",
    text: "A child whose EHCP names a specific school is admitted to that school outside the normal co-ordinated process. The naming process runs separately, through the council's SEN team, and should be settled before the normal offer day. If your child's EHCP is under review or a school is being named, speak to your SEND caseworker rather than following the standard admissions timeline."
  }
];

